{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_17217cf699bfd38da07d8c907d854bedc2b9988e5c42ea3a24eb4fb4b36a1f8e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is installed as an editable package (uv pip install -e .) and uses OpenAI-compatible LLM endpoints configured via API_KEY and BASE_URL environment variables."},{"claim_ids":["clm_44911d8e39912ea551937173f3d00c630abb2092254c023a7f40da446ac470f0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Training via reject_sampling.py runs a multi-round loop: an actor attempts the task, a verifier LLM decides continue/stop, a critic extracts experiences, and an updater writes accepted entries into the experience library JSON."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4efd055c34084012b33c8a01cb98b3fe87b9e67a8c9647c1f619979d0da4deda"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"In FLEX evaluation, the experience library is wrapped via create_memory_retrieval_tool into a tool the Actor can call during reasoning when retrieval is enabled."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6e938a3cc0480141ce1c4634cc6d47c30a94b2cf7c9189cd00425a424d358f3b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"FLEX (Forward Learning from Experience) is a learning paradigm that shifts learning from modifying model parameters to building and leveraging an evolvable experience library."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b60dc02eded538752cf5f0c4d508cc2d7dd860839337fbd0c5563f5b7111b5d1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"test_flex.py exposes CLI flags including --task_type (math/retro), --actor, --memory_path, --split, --samples, --batch_size, --no-retrieve for ablation, --pass_at_n, and --no-telemetry."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c15962b476c4ab7d6489922eb9008d91f09d78b9b16c8c52b034c9f9c9e6e767"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The paper reports experiments on AIME25, USPTO-50k retrosynthesis, and ProteinGym, with improvements such as 40% to 63% on AIME25 and 20% to 30% on USPTO50k."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f7a93818d2994014d6f7ce9c72bd82fae8befabf766903ae6d1a5cdbb122b792"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Core modules include actor.py (task-solving agent), critic.py (experience extraction), explib.py (library abstraction), updater.py (dedup/acceptance), memory_retriever.py, and rate_limiter.py."}],"claim_ids":["clm_17217cf699bfd38da07d8c907d854bedc2b9988e5c42ea3a24eb4fb4b36a1f8e","clm_44911d8e39912ea551937173f3d00c630abb2092254c023a7f40da446ac470f0","clm_4efd055c34084012b33c8a01cb98b3fe87b9e67a8c9647c1f619979d0da4deda","clm_6e938a3cc0480141ce1c4634cc6d47c30a94b2cf7c9189cd00425a424d358f3b","clm_b60dc02eded538752cf5f0c4d508cc2d7dd860839337fbd0c5563f5b7111b5d1","clm_c15962b476c4ab7d6489922eb9008d91f09d78b9b16c8c52b034c9f9c9e6e767","clm_f7a93818d2994014d6f7ce9c72bd82fae8befabf766903ae6d1a5cdbb122b792"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:43:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_eae86e1e9e504c909b2764e9c0665d12","id":"pg_31a237adc6f55dc687cc51661b4f02fd","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/gensi-thuair-flex-readme-md-b749fc351f81-51661b4f02fd.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_84c23c9cbdcd559d93724bcf69c47939"],"title":"GenSI-THUAIR/FLEX/README.md @ b749fc351f81","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:43:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_eae86e1e9e504c909b2764e9c0665d12"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3e91a69bfd6979c28cacf1312f36439b4dbce91ec0da21a77663910322b3ff1d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The retriever exposes multi-level abstraction tools (get_partition_methods, get_partition_rules, get_partition_trajectories), state tools, get_memory_statistics, and a final_answer tool for the actor."},{"claim_ids":["clm_437e55d386afe831d23a86b47988825b88e06ab8f4d26fe6f15e1fb83131e0a7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The memory retriever design prioritizes exhaustive exploration over efficiency, and keeps tools limited to data retrieval while the agent performs semantic analysis and response generation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_525c59aa3d1930d4679511584bfc72bd6de27498e72aac9b48a5e97fac8767e6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each memory entry stores a method description, rules with examples, a revised trajectory with comments, and metadata such as memory_type, problem_category, priority, and timestamps."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6033c9341e04ed26b98d86dd309d4f498e8001edd480496d2e883e08e871e3d8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The retriever agent maintains per-partition exploration state (explored_up_to and recommended_indices) to avoid redundant exploration and support multi-turn continuity."},{"claim_ids":["clm_838ad953422c2926dc31fe65a39fd4f6a9ab9e85177d5a478f6ed8ab0e974c26"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The memory library is partitioned into Golden (successful experiences), Warning (failure cases), and Mixed (learning trajectories) partitions."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3e91a69bfd6979c28cacf1312f36439b4dbce91ec0da21a77663910322b3ff1d","clm_437e55d386afe831d23a86b47988825b88e06ab8f4d26fe6f15e1fb83131e0a7","clm_525c59aa3d1930d4679511584bfc72bd6de27498e72aac9b48a5e97fac8767e6","clm_6033c9341e04ed26b98d86dd309d4f498e8001edd480496d2e883e08e871e3d8","clm_838ad953422c2926dc31fe65a39fd4f6a9ab9e85177d5a478f6ed8ab0e974c26"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:43:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_eae86e1e9e504c909b2764e9c0665d12","id":"pg_5970ef7a015f5da3b98486fa2ccb3185","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/gensi-thuair-flex-docs-memory-retriever-design-md-b749fc351f81-86fa2ccb3185.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_bbd45fcdbeee5d7e80256fff9e4915c2"],"title":"GenSI-THUAIR/FLEX/docs/memory_retriever_design.md @ b749fc351f81","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:43:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_eae86e1e9e504c909b2764e9c0665d12"}
